        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>I have a question regarding what happens with event cards that say Destroy/Remove/Push X in/from a land with Y. If there are multiple lands with Y some of which contain X, must you choose a land with X. Additionally if there are multiple lands with both X and Y but there is an active effect in one of them that will prevent X from being Destroyed/Removed/Pushed, must you target the land without that effect?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>For example let's say I'm playing Stone's Unyielding Defiance, I have played Stubburn Solidarity on a land with both beasts and dehan. There is another land with beasts and dehan. And a third land with only beasts. I am resolving the Overconfidence event card and am at the point where I destroy 1 (dehan) in a land with (beast). Can I</p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n\t<li>Choose to destroy 1 dehan from any of those lands, including the one without dehan I just needed to choose to target a land with beasts. (even though this will have no effect in two of those lands)</li>\r\n\t<li>Choose between the two lands with dehan even though the ones in the land where I played Stubburn Solidarity will not actually be destroyed</li>\r\n\t<li>I have to destroy the dehan in the land that is unprotected&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ol>",
