      {
        "id": 234112,
        "name": "dpt",
        "username": "dpt",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dpt/{size}/1922_2.png",
        "created_at": "2020-10-31T20:52:42.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>\n&gt; If there are multiple lands with Y some of which contain X, must you choose a land with X.\nYes, you must do the effect if you can.</p>\n<p>\n&gt; Additionally if there are multiple lands with both X and Y but there is an active effect in one of them that will prevent X from being Destroyed/Removed/Pushed, must you target the land without that effect?\nYou are free to choose the land where the effect will be prevented.</p>\n<p>So in your question, option 2 is the correct answer.</p>\n<p>(I know this has been discussed extensively, but I'm not sure where the canonical reference is right now.)</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:10:07.142Z",
