        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>\n> If there are multiple lands with Y some of which contain X, must you choose a land with X.\nYes, you must do the effect if you can.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\n> Additionally if there are multiple lands with both X and Y but there is an active effect in one of them that will prevent X from being Destroyed/Removed/Pushed, must you target the land without that effect?\nYou are free to choose the land where the effect will be prevented.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>So in your question, option 2 is the correct answer.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(I know this has been discussed extensively, but I'm not sure where the canonical reference is right now.)</p>",
